From c15fbab508e963909055d598b8fdd4627b978fd6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dipa-studio <183933817+dipa-studio@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 08:11:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add J7 Mali page-table fault diagnostics

The 0322 boot log shows persistent translation faults after resolving BO-table exhaustion. Add a bounded page-table walk and recent BO map/free history to identify the active root or missing mapping on the next boot.

Co-Authored-By: dipa-studio <183933817+dipa-studio@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 A5XELTE_PROGRESS.md                           |   5 +-
 docs/j7prime-bringup.md                       |   5 +-
 xnu/patches/0323-j7prime-g3d-fault-walk.patch | 135 ++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 141 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 xnu/patches/0323-j7prime-g3d-fault-walk.patch

diff --git a/A5XELTE_PROGRESS.md b/A5XELTE_PROGRESS.md
index 7bf2fd5..c81b952 100644
--- a/A5XELTE_PROGRESS.md
+++ b/A5XELTE_PROGRESS.md
@@ -152,5 +152,6 @@ Stage the iPhone 8 Plus userland in an exact-size HFSX USERDATA image, select it
   (… KiB mapped, tables used/total): faultstatus=… mmu_irq=… job_irq=… js_status=…` for the first four faults (AS0+0x1c/
   0x20/0x24, the address matched against the live BO table), and `J7 G3D: client map refused: <why>` naming which of the
   four mapping steps ran out instead of a bare ENOMEM in user space.
-- Not established: any GPU-rendered frame, the lock screen, and the address of that first fault. The next boot's
-  `fault at` line decides between a missing mapping and a wrong pointer in the chain.
+- New boot-log diagnosis: the `CREATE_BO failed (err=12)` lines and the backboardd NULL-BO crash are gone; there is no `crash: sig=` line. The selftest still passes its good rounds (`client round 0/2 (good) status=0 js=00000000`) and rejects its deliberate fault (`status=-3 js=00000008`); unowned-VA submit is rejected and client unmap succeeds. The four observed faults decode as translation faults, not permission faults: low status byte `0xc2`/`0xc3` is translation fault at level 2/3; access bits identify READ/WRITE and bits 31:16 identify source `0x7c10`/`0x7c20`. One fault VA `0x38e2440` is exactly the job-chain head, within BO 11 (`0x38e2000`, 64 KiB); another, `0x3d45000`, is BO 18's first page. The faults recur at the first head while every GPU submit remains `status=-3 js=8` from frame 1; frames 1–3 each report GL work but zero draws in place. There is one `serving user clients` / page-table-pool initialization. The log still shows the Apple logo and no lock screen. This locates the issue in GPU translation/page-table visibility or root selection, but does not establish which one.
+- Patch `0323` adds fault-status words, AS0 TRANSTAB readback vs. `gJ7M.root`, a pool-bounded walk printing `ent/l2/l3/leaf`, and a 16-entry map/free event ring (`recent` lines) to distinguish stale/missing mappings from a wrong root or VA. It is generated from the reconstructed source; its `git apply --check` validation passes against the 0322 reconstruction. No source-level cause is claimed yet.
+- Not established: a GPU-rendered frame, the lock screen, or why the GPU walker faults. The next boot log should include `J7 G3D: walk transtab=...` and `J7 G3D: recent ...` lines; those will distinguish a wrong root/table from a missing leaf or BO lifetime issue.
diff --git a/docs/j7prime-bringup.md b/docs/j7prime-bringup.md
index 678e1d7..0a826d8 100644
--- a/docs/j7prime-bringup.md
+++ b/docs/j7prime-bringup.md
@@ -145,5 +145,6 @@ published with the ios-root release as `sweetgl-extents.txt`.
      good rounds pass), so nothing on the panel was drawn by the GPU - the logo is iBoot's;
   2. after ~6 minutes CREATE_BO returns ENOMEM and backboardd dies in Mesa's `submit_batch` on the NULL BO. The kernel
      BO table was 64 entries and CoreAnimation maps one per IOSurface.
-- `0322` raises the table to 512 and makes the next log say what the fault was about (`J7 G3D: fault at <address> in bo
-  N of M (…, tables u/t)`) and why a map was refused, instead of only `-3` and a bare ENOMEM.
+- `0322` raises the table to 512 and adds the initial fault address/BO report and map-refusal reason.
+- **Next boot-log result:** the BO-table exhaustion and backboardd NULL-BO crash are gone; the selftest's valid submission passes, while all actual submits still fail `-3 js=8`. The reported VAs include `0x38e2440`, the job-chain head in BO 11, and `0x3d45000`, BO 18's first page. Correctly decoded Mali status bytes `0xc2`/`0xc3` indicate level-2/level-3 translation faults (READ/WRITE), with source IDs `0x7c10`/`0x7c20`. A single pool initialization is logged. No GPU frame or lock screen has been observed; root/table visibility remains unresolved.
+- `0323` adds TRANSTAB readback, a bounds-checked page-table walk for the fault VA, decoded fault fields, and a 16-entry successful BO map/free ring. It applies cleanly to the reconstructed source including 0322. On the next boot, pull `J7 G3D: walk transtab=...` and `J7 G3D: recent ...` lines to determine whether the root, table chain, leaf, or BO lifetime is wrong.
diff --git a/xnu/patches/0323-j7prime-g3d-fault-walk.patch b/xnu/patches/0323-j7prime-g3d-fault-walk.patch
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..b820c90
--- /dev/null
+++ b/xnu/patches/0323-j7prime-g3d-fault-walk.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,135 @@
+From: j7 g3d
+Subject: [PATCH] j7prime: diagnose G3D page-table faults
+
+Decode Mali MMU fault status, read back AS0's translation-table root, safely walk
+our page-table pool for the faulting VA, and print recent BO map/free events.
+
+--- a/iokit/Kernel/arm/A5XELTEGPU.cpp
++++ b/iokit/Kernel/arm/A5XELTEGPU.cpp
+@@ -322,6 +322,18 @@ struct J7MaliBo {
+     bool used;
+ };
+
++/* A short history of BO lifetimes, printed with the next fault.  A translation fault inside a
++ * mapped BO means the GPU's walk found nothing where this driver wrote a leaf; whether that range
++ * was just mapped, freed or re-used tells a lost mapping apart from a range that was never ours. */
++#define J7M_EVENTS      16
++
++struct J7MEvent {
++    uint64_t va;
++    uint64_t size;
++    uint32_t slot;
++    char kind;                      /* 'k' kernel BO, 'm' client map, 'f' free */
++};
++
+ static struct {
+     vm_offset_t gpu;
+     IOBufferMemoryDescriptor *pool;
+@@ -336,6 +348,8 @@ static struct {
+     bool inflight;
+     uint32_t inflightSlot;
+     struct J7MaliBo bos[J7M_MAX_BOS];
++    struct J7MEvent events[J7M_EVENTS];
++    uint32_t eventHead;
+ } gJ7M;
+
+ static uint64_t *
+@@ -344,6 +358,17 @@ j7m_table(uint64_t pa)
+     return reinterpret_cast<uint64_t *>(gJ7M.poolVA + (pa - gJ7M.poolPA));
+ }
+
++static void
++j7m_note(char kind, unsigned slot, uint64_t va, uint64_t size)
++{
++    struct J7MEvent *e = &gJ7M.events[gJ7M.eventHead % J7M_EVENTS];
++    gJ7M.eventHead++;
++    e->kind = kind;
++    e->slot = slot;
++    e->va = va;
++    e->size = size;
++}
++
+ /* PA of a new zeroed 4 KiB table, or 0. */
+ static uint64_t
+ j7m_table_new(void)
+@@ -573,12 +598,14 @@ j7m_bo_new(uint64_t size)
+     bo->va = va;
+     bo->size = size;
+     bo->used = true;
++    j7m_note('k', static_cast<unsigned>(bo - gJ7M.bos) + 1, va, size);
+     return bo;
+ }
+
+ static void
+ j7m_bo_free(struct J7MaliBo *bo)
+ {
++    j7m_note('f', static_cast<unsigned>(bo - gJ7M.bos) + 1, bo->va, bo->size);
+     for (uint64_t u = 0; u < bo->size; u += J7M_PAGE) {
+         j7m_unmap_page(bo->va + u);
+     }
+@@ -635,6 +662,12 @@ j7m_fault_report(uint32_t jobIRQ, uint32_t mmuIRQ)
+     }
+     const uint64_t fault = ((uint64_t)a5g3d_read32(gJ7M.gpu, J7M_AS0 + 0x24) << 32) |
+         a5g3d_read32(gJ7M.gpu, J7M_AS0 + 0x20);
++    const uint32_t fs = a5g3d_read32(gJ7M.gpu, J7M_AS0 + 0x1c);
++    const unsigned status = fs & 0xff;
++    const unsigned level = status & 3;
++    const unsigned access = (fs >> 8) & 3;
++    const char *faultKind = (status & 0xfc) == 0xc0 ? "translation" : "other";
++    const char *accessKind = access == 1 ? "execute" : access == 2 ? "read" : access == 3 ? "write" : "unknown";
+     uint64_t mapped = 0;
+     unsigned used = 0, inside = 0;
+     for (unsigned i = 0; i < J7M_MAX_BOS; i++) {
+@@ -648,11 +681,43 @@ j7m_fault_report(uint32_t jobIRQ, uint32_t mmuIRQ)
+             inside = i + 1;
+         }
+     }
++
++    const uint64_t transtab = ((uint64_t)a5g3d_read32(gJ7M.gpu, J7M_AS0 + 0x04) << 32) |
++        a5g3d_read32(gJ7M.gpu, J7M_AS0 + 0x00);
++    uint64_t ent[4] = { 0, 0, 0, 0 };
++    bool walkOK = gJ7M.poolVA && gJ7M.poolPA && gJ7M.poolTables;
++    uint64_t table = transtab & 0x0000fffffffff000ULL;
++    const unsigned shifts[3] = { 39, 30, 21 };
++    const uint64_t poolEnd = gJ7M.poolPA + (uint64_t)gJ7M.poolTables * J7M_PAGE;
++    for (unsigned i = 0; walkOK && i < 4; i++) {
++        if (table < gJ7M.poolPA || table > poolEnd - J7M_PAGE || (table & (J7M_PAGE - 1))) {
++            walkOK = false;
++            break;
++        }
++        const unsigned shift = i < 3 ? shifts[i] : 12;
++        ent[i] = j7m_table(table)[(fault >> shift) & 0x1ff];
++        if (i < 3) {
++            if (!(ent[i] & 1)) {
++                break;
++            }
++            table = ent[i] & 0x0000fffffffff000ULL;
++        }
++    }
+     IOLog("J7 G3D: fault at %llx in bo %u of %u (%llu KiB mapped, tables %u/%u): "
+-        "faultstatus=%08x mmu_irq=%08x job_irq=%08x js_status=%08x\n",
++        "faultstatus=%08x (%s level %u %s source=%x) mmu_irq=%08x job_irq=%08x js_status=%08x\n",
+         (unsigned long long)fault, inside, used, (unsigned long long)(mapped / 1024),
+-        gJ7M.poolUsed, gJ7M.poolTables, a5g3d_read32(gJ7M.gpu, J7M_AS0 + 0x1c),
++        gJ7M.poolUsed, gJ7M.poolTables, fs, faultKind, level, accessKind, fs >> 16,
+         mmuIRQ, jobIRQ, a5g3d_read32(gJ7M.gpu, J7M_JS(gJ7M.inflightSlot) + 0x24));
++    IOLog("J7 G3D: walk transtab=%llx root=%llx valid=%u ent=%llx l2=%llx l3=%llx leaf=%llx\n",
++        (unsigned long long)transtab, (unsigned long long)gJ7M.root, walkOK,
++        (unsigned long long)ent[0], (unsigned long long)ent[1],
++        (unsigned long long)ent[2], (unsigned long long)ent[3]);
++    const uint32_t n = gJ7M.eventHead < J7M_EVENTS ? gJ7M.eventHead : J7M_EVENTS;
++    for (uint32_t i = 0; i < n; i++) {
++        const struct J7MEvent &e = gJ7M.events[(gJ7M.eventHead - n + i) % J7M_EVENTS];
++        IOLog("J7 G3D: recent %c bo=%u va=%llx size=%llx\n", e.kind, e.slot,
++            (unsigned long long)e.va, (unsigned long long)e.size);
++    }
+ }
+
+ /* Poll for completion. 0 = done OK, -1 = timeout, -2 = job fault, -3 = MMU fault. */
+@@ -1019,5 +1084,6 @@ j7m_map_user(IOMemoryDescriptor *md, void *owner)
+     bo->start = va;
+     bo->size = size;
+     bo->used = true;
++    j7m_note('m', static_cast<unsigned>(bo - gJ7M.bos) + 1, va, size);
+     return bo;
+ }
-- 
2.43.0

